Vikram and Betal: The Kind King

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a king who was very kind to his people,” said Betal. “He always wanted everyone in his kingdom to be happy.”

One day, the king decided to test his people.

He placed a large stone in the middle of the road and hid nearby.

Many people passed by.

Some complained about the stone but walked around it.

No one tried to remove it.

After some time, a poor farmer came along.

He saw the stone and thought, “This might hurt someone.”

He struggled but finally pushed the stone aside.

Under the stone, he found a bag of gold coins.

There was also a note from the king that said, “This reward is for the person who thinks of others.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the farmer get the reward?”

Vikram replied, “Because he cared about others, not just himself.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Helping others brings rewards.
